n4. \"并通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\" - this is a partial sentence. The full sentence is \"仓管裴小棠把这批货从\"待发\"改成\"报损\"，并通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车。\" The evidence should be a continuous substring. \"并通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\" is a continuous substring. ✓\n5. \"司机回了一句\"知道了\"\" - 1 sentence ✓\n6. \"便把已经发动的货车熄了火\" - 1 sentence (partial of \"司机回了一句\"知道了\"，便把已经发动的货车熄了火。\") ✓\n7. \"渗出水顺着托盘流到地面\" - 1 sentence ✓\n8. \"裴小棠又去拿拖把\" - 1 sentence ✓\n\nAll good. Let me write the final JSON.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider fact #4. The subject \"并通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\" - the \"并\" connects to the previous clause, so the subject is still 裴小棠. The evidence doesn't show 裴小棠 explicitly but the context makes it clear. The fact statement does include 裴小棠. Is this OK?\n\nLooking at the rules: \"两句内无法同时证明主体、来源和事实时，改写、拆分或删除候选，不能让 speaker 代替正文证据。\"\n\nThe evidence \"并通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\" doesn't explicitly show 裴小棠 as the subject, but the \"并\" refers back to the previous clause. This is a grammatical continuation. I think this is acceptable since the \"并\" clearly indicates the same subject.\n\nAlternatively, I could use a longer evidence: \"仓管裴小棠把这批货从\"待发\"改成\"报损\"，并通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\" - but this would be evidence for both facts #3 and #4. Each fact should have its own evidence.\n\nLet me think... The current evidence for #4 is \"并通知司机取消下午那趟去港东批发市场的车\" which is a continuous substring and the subject can be inferred from \"并\". I think this is fine.\n\nSame issue for #6: \"便把已经发动的货车熄了火\" - \"便\" connects to the previous clause, so the subject is 司机. The fact statement says \"司机将已发动的货车熄了火\" which matches. Acceptable.\n\nOK, finalizing. Let me also check - is there any info about the time? \"午前\" (before noon). I have this in fact #1.\n\nAre there any因果关系 I should record? \"冷库温控器跳闸 → 荔枝渗水\" is a clear cause-effect. I could add a fact: \"冷库温控器跳闸导致整箱荔枝渗水\" or similar. But the rules say to keep facts as one core assertion. The connection is implicit in the text sequence. I think keeping them as separate facts with the se